WEBVTT

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:15.510
Izayoi.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:18.850
You idiot civilians
will put everyone in danger.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:20.100
Ango.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:24.230
Karita.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:34.450
If the tick had already gotten to them,
then it would be too late.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:39.330
It's also possible that it found its way
onto smaller animals, like mice.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:40.910
Let's go.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.000
Getting involved with them
would be foolish.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.420
What is the matter with all of you?

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.630
Ms. Hana, don't.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:52.170
How can you go around this world,
shooting people with your guns?

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.010
Izayoi! Hang in there!

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:59.050
Ms. Ran, are you all right?

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.520
Izayoi.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.310
Was I able to be of some help?

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.310
I can't face Arashi otherwise.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.320
Arashi?

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.150
There was a time...

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:17.160
when I tried to kill all of you
with poison.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:20.030
I'm so sorry for that, but...

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.000
he stopped me back then

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.830
and told me I could make up for it
if I stayed alive.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:28.960
<i>Arashi did?</i>

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:34.880
I was going to be more useful
to the team from that time on.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.220
How frustrating.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:40.970
Ms. Kurumi...

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:44.980
Please take care of yourself.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:53.480
They called us "civilians."

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:55.530
Who the hell are they?

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:32.750
SUMMER SOLSTICE

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.040
Boy, I'm beat.

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:37.800
Is Team Spring's camp much farther?

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:43.430
Ms. Hana, something is wrong.

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:44.340
What?

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:50.230
Team Spring's camp is gone.

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:55.440
Fujiko! Tsunomata! Where are you?

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.570
Chisa! Momota!

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:00.360
We would like to let Kurumi get some rest.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.900
Oh, I'm doing okay.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.410
Don't push yourself.

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:08.830
Then let's go further inland
to the area that I used to camp at.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:10.910
It will keep the wind and rain off us.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:15.750
Where did everyone go?

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:21.420
We're going to crash!

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:22.920
Natsu, steer to port!

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:25.260
This way?

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:36.100
We made it.

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:38.320
Gosh, that was way too close.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:43.490
But, man, Kyushu is so far away.
I wonder if those guys are still alive?

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:46.820
They've got Ms. Botan with them,
so I'm sure they're fine.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:49.830
I thought I saw a person just now...

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:52.660
A person? You sure it wasn't a tree?

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:56.330
It's a person.
There's a person in the water!

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:58.000
Let's lower the boat.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.210
Stop the ship!

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:06.050
Isn't that Hotaru?

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:08.140
I guess she kind of looks like her,

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:09.850
but doesn't she seem a little different?

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.060
It's faint, but she's breathing.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:14.640
Natsu, get her a change of clothes.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.560
Oh, sure.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:24.190
The ship is rocking.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:29.530
Hotaru?

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:34.540
Hotaru? Where are you?

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:37.420
We have to raise anchor
before the ship capsizes.

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.750
Arashi, I can't find Hotaru.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:40.960
What?

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.090
Hotaru!

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:45.420
Oh, over there.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.480
Are you Hotaru?

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:57.810
My name is Hibari.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:05:59.600
Hibari Niigusa.

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:02.770
-She's on the verge of death.
-What?

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.530
Hotaru is...

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.200
on the verge of death.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:09.700
The other people with her as well.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:11.950
They're all on the verge of death.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:16.200
Hibari?

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:18.750
Are you alive over there, Chimaki?

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:21.630
I'm still alive,
but I'm about to die from boredom.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:24.920
<i>How many days has it been
since we fell down here?</i>

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:27.220
Ms. Botan!

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.590
I'm going to go find some help!

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:32.220
Whose help? There's nobody here!

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.140
You never know, there might be.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:48.070
What a pretty lady.

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:49.450
How are you feeling?

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:52.030
Do you remember who you are?

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:55.700
I'm Momota from Team Spring.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:07:00.710
He needs something warm and soft to eat.

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:02.290
I already made this.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:04.920
It's a soup made from mashed up mushrooms.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:13.260
Hey, are the mushrooms okay?

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:19.850
You've got a lot of scratches.
I'll put some medicine on them.

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:33.320
Why are you putting something different
on each one?

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:35.530
Because they all have different effects.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:37.120
Hey...

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:38.620
Hey, Madonna.

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:41.790
Shigeru?

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:44.500
Is that you? You're still alive!

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:49.800
Wait. Who are you?

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:54.550
Oh, I'm a member of Team Spring.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:56.930
You're from one of the civilian teams.

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:04.600
It hurts. My stomach really hurts.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:07.400
Are you okay? You have a fever, too.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.150
I feel sick.

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:11.780
The scratches on your arm are swelling.

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:14.990
But your other injuries are okay.

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:17.490
Your knee healed particularly fast.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:20.660
I'll get some fresh water, so wait here.

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:22.750
I'll cool your forehead with it.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:24.080
Okay.

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:31.170
Where's the bathroom?

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:34.130
Miss...

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:37.680
Ban, that root we used for food
is no good.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.600
It's causing stomach problems.

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:41.730
As for the herbs we tried on his injuries,

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:44.140
B doesn't work, but D does.

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:47.480
Hey, I think we should stop doing this.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:49.690
Stop? And then do what?

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:51.530
Who's going to try them?

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:54.240
Someone has to try the food and medicine.

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:58.450
It's okay.

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:00.490
The moon isn't watching us.

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:07.880
<i>She wasn't a nice lady after all.</i>

00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:10.460
<i>What is this place?
They're going to kill me.</i>

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:13.300
<i>If I stay here, I'll be killed.</i>

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:25.390
<i>The guy with white hair.</i>

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:27.560
Shigeru...

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:29.400
You really are here.

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:38.740
So, this is where you went.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:45.620
There are a lot of caves
like this in the area.

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:46.920
Seems like a good spot.

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:49.540
First, let's gather some food
and firewood.

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:51.630
Get some rest, Kurumi.

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:53.130
Thanks.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.380
So far, it's been okay,

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:59.640
but we can't be sure if this area is safe.

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:00.890
You're right.

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:03.680
All that falling ash in the west
caught us off guard.

00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:07.310
In other words,
there's no place that's 100% safe.

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:12.820
Thank you, Fubuki and Miss Mitsuru.

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:14.570
What's this?

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:19.740
It looks like it was bitten to death.

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:24.370
From the bite marks, it looks like
a group of small animals ganged up on it.

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:26.960
There must be dangerous animals
around here.

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:33.920
That's Momota's sneaker.

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:36.130
Where did you find it? Show us.

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:42.470
Rain. Nothing but rain lately.

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:48.140
What's that sound? That's quite an echo.

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:01.160
The trees have turned to charcoal.

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:11.330
They produce this sound
because they've become so hard.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:36.320
It's those punks.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:41.150
Found him.
Or at least, I think that's him.

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:43.110
Excuse me, please let me look.

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:49.500
-Momota.
-Ms. Hana.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.460
Something is out there.

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:09.310
<i>Why do we have to defend ourselves
from humans in this world as well?</i>

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:16.860
From the looks of it, they're using him
as live bait to lure animals.

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:18.150
What do you think?

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:21.190
Are they likely to return him
if we walk up to them and ask?

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:22.360
No way.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.950
They shot and killed a defenseless man
like it was nothing.

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:27.990
I would love to get revenge for Izayoi,

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:31.830
but I have no intention of killing
or getting killed myself.

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:35.750
They've made quite the impressive
tree house.

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:38.840
It's got running water, and I see
smoke coming from the kitchen.

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:42.340
At the very least,
we know they're not insane.

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:47.050
As far as construction and engineering,
they have professional knowledge.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:50.220
Do you know a lot
about construction, Ms. Ran?

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:53.020
I used to run an architecture school.

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:55.850
You know,
Akiwo was a venture company president.

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:03.320
A hang glider?

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:05.070
We didn't get equipment like that.

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:10.160
Sakuya, I want you to find out
where that glider is going.

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:11.160
What?

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:13.120
Go after it. Hurry.

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:14.330
Oh, right.

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:22.090
What's that? I hear some kind of music.

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:35.730
Was that music?

00:13:37.190 --> 00:13:38.440
Oh, yes.

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:44.530
I was trying to play
Chopin's "Prelude Op. 28, No. 7."

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:06.470
It's about to start raining.

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:13.890
She just rode an updraft.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:20.610
<i>I lost sight of it.</i>

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:22.610
Ms. Ran is going to be pissed at me.

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:26.400
Found you.

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:33.370
Shigeru...

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:38.580
You're wandering around again?

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:42.040
Ango, are you all right?

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:45.590
Why so serious, Ryo?
I was just taking a walk.

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:47.420
Hey, Ango.

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:50.180
You remember
what all the professors told us, right?

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:55.310
Your team name will be "Summer."

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:59.940
There will also be three civilian teams,
"Spring," "Winter," and "Autumn."

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:03.400
Your team will be the best among them.

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:05.230
You've all undergone training.

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:11.530
You must protect, manage, and guide
the others, and punish them if necessary.

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:16.700
We weren't actually going to do
what they said, but we still can.

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:20.290
Let's gather them all together
and show them how it's done.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:24.210
We'll make them understand why
they're here and the importance of...

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:25.710
being the chosen ones.

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:32.470
Their set-up is flawless.

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:36.100
There's always someone watching
who comes and goes.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:39.810
They constantly keep in communication,
and they always eat together.

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:43.940
Furthermore,
they hardly allow for any downtime.

00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:48.990
Then we wait for an opportunity to climb
the cliff and take Momota back by force.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:52.110
I'll do it.

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:54.450
I'll draw them away.

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:59.370
I'll create smoke in the forest
on the other side while you climb up.

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:02.540
-But that puts you in danger, Mr. Aramaki.
-You'll be in more danger, Ms. Hana.

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:04.920
We need to use teamwork here.

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:07.460
I'll take action independently.

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:16.050
Smoke!

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:20.100
There's a fire!

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:21.270
It's close!

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:22.270
Now is my chance.

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:28.020
Hold on, Momota. I'm coming.

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:31.900
I've worked out most of the notes.

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:33.780
I'll try some different songs today.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:46.420
Momota!

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:48.630
Momota!

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:51.010
Momota!

00:16:53.720 --> 00:16:54.590
Be quiet.

00:16:58.680 --> 00:16:59.970
It's okay. Relax.

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:02.350
I'll carry you on my back. Let's hurry.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.140
Just like I thought.

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:07.440
<i>It's that guy,</i>

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:09.770
<i>the one who shot and killed Mr. Izayoi.</i>

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:11.940
Hana, was that your name?

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:14.780
Was that smoke your way of luring us away?

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:19.490
Sorry, but we never let everyone
do the same thing.

00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:22.500
I'm taking Momota back with me.

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:24.290
Take him back?

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:28.130
We took him in after he washed up.
We fed him and nursed him.

00:17:28.750 --> 00:17:31.050
You also used him as bait to lure animals.

00:17:31.670 --> 00:17:33.590
That's just how he earned his keep.

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:36.970
Hello down there!

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:39.470
Members of Team Summer A!

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:42.770
We have one of your friends!

00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:44.680
It's the flying girl!

00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:50.360
We would like to trade her for the member
of Team Spring you've got!

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:53.070
We don't want any trouble!

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:55.440
Let's resolve this peacefully!

00:17:56.030 --> 00:17:57.910
We look forward to your response!

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:04.080
What have you done to Koruri?
Where is she?

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:08.620
<i>I have to make sure
this doesn't turn into a forest fire.</i>

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:10.080
What's wrong?

00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:11.960
What is it?

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:16.340
Fubuki! Miss Mitsuru!

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:29.810
Tell me where Koruri is!

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:32.820
If anything happens to her,
I'll kill every last one of you!

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:34.980
As if you haven't already done far worse!

00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:41.070
We won't stand to see any of our friends
bullied or killed by the likes of you!

00:18:42.910 --> 00:18:45.200
You civilians don't know your place!

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:47.330
I have no idea
who you think you are, but--

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:48.620
Ango!

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:50.040
They're coming.

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:55.460
What the... They're biting me!

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:57.720
Get inside the hut! Hurry!

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:05.180
They're coming in
through the windows. Shit!

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:06.930
Momota, keep your head down.

00:19:07.930 --> 00:19:09.190
Damn these things!

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:11.730
They're bats?

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:17.820
-Were you trying to hit me?
-No!

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:21.530
Bats chase after things that fall
because they think it's prey.

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:23.200
My father told me that once.

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:26.080
I'll go outside and throw
sticks and branches.

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:28.580
That will keep them from coming in here.

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:30.250
Kill the ones left inside.

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:33.750
She just gave us orders.

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:36.050
She got the better of us, Ango.

00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:45.640
I should have brought
that boomerang with me.

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:52.350
Burn more fresh branches!
Drive them off with the smoke!

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:53.730
I'm already on it!

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:55.690
Are you all right?

00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:58.480
I'm fine, but my dogs...

00:19:59.070 --> 00:20:01.280
We can treat you. Come back to our camp.

00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:02.360
What?

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:05.070
You too, doggies. Please follow me.

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:12.250
Those bats completely lost their eyes
and all color on their bodies.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:15.960
They must have survived by staying
underground during the brief ice age.

00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:19.920
They must be using echolocation
to find prey.

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:23.260
That explains why people
who stay still manage to survive.

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:28.180
<i>I thought they were just overbearing jerks
who killed without remorse.</i>

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:32.770
<i>But here they are, giving us first aid.
Who exactly are these people?</i>

00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:35.520
More importantly, where is Koruri?

00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:37.270
Give her back!

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:42.950
You don't have to tie her up.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:46.240
She may be cute,
but she's a member of Team Summer A.

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:48.280
That means she might be ruthless.

00:20:49.990 --> 00:20:51.870
Is it the anemia again, Kurumi?

00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:53.040
Any morning sickness?

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:55.790
No. I'm fine.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:58.130
Is there anything I can do, Kurumi?

00:20:58.540 --> 00:20:59.800
I'll do whatever you need.

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:03.050
I'm all right. Don't worry too much.

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:08.600
Warming and massaging your feet is best.

00:21:08.680 --> 00:21:11.220
What are you doing? Don't touch her!

00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:16.020
If you ask Ban, he can teach you
breathing techniques and maternity yoga.

00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:17.730
He also has iron supplements.

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:20.610
How dare you!
You killed Mr. Izayoi in cold blood!

00:21:20.860 --> 00:21:22.400
He was a good man!

00:21:26.570 --> 00:21:27.570
What are these things?

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:30.080
Ouch! They bit me!

00:21:32.240 --> 00:21:33.450
I'll untie you now.

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:37.670
Just so you know, I didn't lure you to us.

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:39.210
I know.

00:21:43.670 --> 00:21:45.800
Is everyone okay?

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:47.380
No, I'm not.

00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:48.340
Akane?

00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:51.390
Akane is in trouble. She's bleeding!

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:54.310
This time, I won't let anyone die.

00:21:55.430 --> 00:21:56.690
Breathe slowly.

00:21:56.770 --> 00:21:58.520
Not from your chest,
but from your stomach.

00:21:58.600 --> 00:22:00.150
Easy now. Stay calm.

00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:02.650
Breathe in and out through your nose.

00:22:04.990 --> 00:22:06.650
I'll go and get Ban.

00:22:08.070 --> 00:22:09.320
You're letting her go?

00:22:09.990 --> 00:22:11.530
So what if she goes?
